{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And there is no sense in saying <b>\"Leave Me alone\"</b> and I will become angry, for if His anger had not yet burned, how would His anger burn after Moses leaves Him alone? Rather, the way of the peshat is that He says: leave Me alone, and I will consume them in My wrath, in the manner of \"Let Me alone, that I may destroy them\" (Deuteronomy 9:14). And by way of truth, [it means:] relinquish mercy, and My attribute of justice will contend against them, and I will consume them through it, for in My presence it has no authority over them. And this is the sense of <b>\"And Moses implored the face of YHWH his Elohim\"</b> — and it is like the sense of \"before the Master, Adonai, the Elohim of Israel\" (Exodus 34:23). And thus he mentioned in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 9:26) YHWH (ה') with alef-dalet and yod-heh after it. And it is possible that \"וַיְחַל\" is from the root of תְּחִלָּה (beginning), and the enlightened will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:19:51.381782004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}